{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_privacy_boundary_pattern", "label": "Privacy boundary: LLM sees schema, never raw data", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/Enterprise-Chatbot-Porting-Findings.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every structured-data engagement (Gordian, FinFrock, Axiom) independently converged on the same architecture so a tenant's raw dataset is never sent to the LLM, only schema/column descriptions/metadata; the model generates an operation (SQL or Pandas expression) that a deterministic runtime executes against the real data outside the model. Valuable commercially, not just technically: it lets InApp tell a client 'your dataset is not passed to the LLM.'"}, {"id": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_generate_then_execute_pattern", "label": "Generate-then-execute pattern", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/Enterprise-Chatbot-Porting-Findings.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gordian (Pandas), FinFrock (SQL) and Axiom (SQL) all have the model emit a program rather than an answer; a deterministic runtime produces the number. Chosen because it eliminates arithmetic hallucination and makes every answer reproducible and auditable."}, {"id": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_schema_metadata_catalogue_gap", "label": "Schema metadata catalogue gap (Phase 1.1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/Enterprise-Chatbot-Porting-Findings.md", "source_location": "\u00a74, \u00a75 Phase 1.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "WHITELISTED_TABLES is a hardcoded Python dict of bare column names with no descriptions, relationships, per-tenant indexing, or search \u2014 identified as the single biggest structural gap versus Axiom's per-tenant indexed schema catalogue approach, and named as the highest-leverage fix because it unblocks confidence scoring, tabular ingestion, and the external-database connector."}, {"id": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_gordian_engagement", "label": "Gordian engagement (proposals, RBAC, Pandas + graphs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/Enterprise-Chatbot-Porting-Findings.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_axiom_engagement", "label": "Axiom engagement (multi-tenant schema-aware SQL at scale)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/Enterprise-Chatbot-Porting-Findings.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_finfrock_engagement", "label": "FinFrock engagement (deterministic text-to-SQL)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/Enterprise-Chatbot-Porting-Findings.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_external_tenant_db_connector", "label": "External tenant database connector (Phase 3.3)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/Enterprise-Chatbot-Porting-Findings.md", "source_location": "\u00a75 Phase 3.3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Generalise the SQL path into a connector pointing at a tenant's own database rather than only the platform schema. Highest ceiling and largest security surface in the set, deliberately gated to start only after the schema metadata catalogue (1.1) and query validation/confidence scoring (1.2) are proven in production on the platform's own schema."}, {"id": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_integration_plan", "label": "Integration plan (Phase 1/2/3 ordering)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/Enterprise-Chatbot-Porting-Findings.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ordered by (value x fit with what the platform already has) / effort, so each item plugs into an existing seam (ToolRegistry, pending_clarification, SQL path) rather than requiring the chat graph to be re-architected."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_gordian_engagement", "target": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_generate_then_execute_pattern", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/Enterprise-Chatbot-Porting-Findings.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.2", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_axiom_engagement", "target": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_generate_then_execute_pattern", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/Enterprise-Chatbot-Porting-Findings.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.2", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_finfrock_engagement", "target": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_generate_then_execute_pattern", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/Enterprise-Chatbot-Porting-Findings.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.2", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_gordian_engagement", "target": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_privacy_boundary_pattern", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/Enterprise-Chatbot-Porting-Findings.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_axiom_engagement", "target": "docs_enterprise_chatbot_porting_findings_privacy_boundary_pattern", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRAC